   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a7ebf693",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Building Defect AI — Notebook workflow\n",
    "\n",
    "Run from the repository root. Expected data layout: `dataset/BD3_split/{train,val,test}/<class_name>/...`.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Task:** classify images into the seven BD3 labels. This notebook records the method, why it is used, the result and its interpretation. Do not treat model predictions as professional inspection findings."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "1ce10977",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Project root: d:\\02_LEARNING\\03_Courses\\04_Hope AI & Data Science Course\\00_Sessions\\Week11-Deep Learning Module\\Building_Defect_AI\n",
      "Dataset: d:\\02_LEARNING\\03_Courses\\04_Hope AI & Data Science Course\\00_Sessions\\Week11-Deep Learning Module\\Building_Defect_AI\\dataset\\BD3_split\n",
      "Model: d:\\02_LEARNING\\03_Courses\\04_Hope AI & Data Science Course\\00_Sessions\\Week11-Deep Learning Module\\Building_Defect_AI\\models\\building_defect_resnet18_experiment3.pth\n",
      "Device: cuda\n",
      "\n",
      "Project paths verified successfully.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "\n",
    "# Automatically identify the project root\n",
    "CURRENT_DIR = Path.cwd()\n",
    "\n",
    "if CURRENT_DIR.name == \"notebooks\":\n",
    "    ROOT = CURRENT_DIR.parent\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    ROOT = CURRENT_DIR\n",
    "\n",
    "# Project paths\n",
    "DATA = ROOT / \"dataset\" / \"BD3_split\"\n",
    "MODEL_PATH = ROOT / \"models\" / \"building_defect_resnet18_experiment3.pth\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Select device\n",
    "DEVICE = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Project root:\", ROOT)\n",
    "print(\"Dataset:\", DATA)\n",
    "print(\"Model:\", MODEL_PATH)\n",
    "print(\"Device:\", DEVICE)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Verify paths\n",
    "assert DATA.exists(), f\"Dataset not found: {DATA}\"\n",
    "assert MODEL_PATH.exists(), f\"Model checkpoint not found: {MODEL_PATH}\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nProject paths verified successfully.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cc63bec6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Evaluate the selected checkpoint on the held-out test set\n",
    "\n",
    "This is the final performance estimate. Do not use the test set to tune hyperparameters. The checkpoint is expected to contain `model_state_dict`, `num_classes`, `class_names`, as saved by the project training scripts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "60a7328b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Test accuracy: 87.9245%\n",
      "              precision    recall  f1-score   support\n",
      "\n",
      "       algae     0.9528    0.9758    0.9641       124\n",
      " major_crack     0.7656    0.8448    0.8033       116\n",
      " minor_crack     0.8878    0.6905    0.7768       126\n",
      "     peeling     0.8868    0.9038    0.8952       104\n",
      "       plain     0.9213    0.9750    0.9474       120\n",
      "    spalling     0.8158    0.9300    0.8692       100\n",
      "       stain     0.9368    0.8476    0.8900       105\n",
      "\n",
      "    accuracy                         0.8792       795\n",
      "   macro avg     0.8810    0.8811    0.8780       795\n",
      "weighted avg     0.8824    0.8792    0.8777       795\n",
      "\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import torch.nn as nn\n",
    "from torch.utils.data import DataLoader\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import classification_report, confusion_matrix, accuracy_score\n",
    "CKPT = ROOT / \"models\" / \"building_defect_resnet18_experiment3.pth\"\n",
    "assert CKPT.exists(), f\"Copy the Experiment 3 checkpoint to {CKPT}\"\n",
    "checkpoint = torch.load(CKPT, map_location=DEVICE, weights_only=True)\n",
    "class_names = checkpoint[\"class_names\"]\n",
    "model = models.resnet18(weights=None)\n",
    "model.fc = nn.Linear(model.fc.in_features, checkpoint[\"num_classes\"])\n",
    "model.load_state_dict(checkpoint[\"model_state_dict\"])\n",
    "model.to(DEVICE).eval()\n",
    "test_ds = datasets.ImageFolder(DATA / \"test\", transform=models.ResNet18_Weights.DEFAULT.transforms())\n",
    "assert test_ds.classes == class_names, (test_ds.classes, class_names)\n",
    "test_loader = DataLoader(test_ds, batch_size=16, shuffle=False, num_workers=0)\n",
    "y_true, y_pred = [], []\n",
    "with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "    for x, y in test_loader:\n",
    "        pred = model(x.to(DEVICE)).argmax(1).cpu().tolist()\n",
    "        y_pred.extend(pred); y_true.extend(y.tolist())\n",
    "print(\"Test accuracy:\", f\"{accuracy_score(y_true, y_pred):.4%}\")\n",
    "print(classification_report(y_true, y_pred, target_names=class_names, digits=4))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "26011873",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Confusion matrix\n",
    "\n",
    "Rows are actual classes and columns are predicted classes. Off-diagonal values show which categories are confused. Inspect crack classes carefully because missing a major crack may have higher practical consequence than confusing two visually similar surface categories."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "b922cc10",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 900x700 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "cm = confusion_matrix(y_true, y_pred)\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(9,7))\n",
    "sns.heatmap(cm, annot=True, fmt=\"d\", cmap=\"Blues\", xticklabels=class_names, yticklabels=class_names)\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Predicted\"); plt.ylabel(\"Actual\"); plt.title(\"Experiment 3 — test confusion matrix\")\n",
    "plt.xticks(rotation=35, ha=\"right\"); plt.yticks(rotation=0); plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "out = ROOT / \"outputs\" / \"figures\"; out.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "plt.savefig(out / \"experiment3_test_confusion_matrix.png\", dpi=180, bbox_inches=\"tight\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "108df9c3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Test accuracy: 87.9245%\n",
      "Test images: 795\n",
      "Results saved: d:\\02_LEARNING\\03_Courses\\04_Hope AI & Data Science Course\\00_Sessions\\Week11-Deep Learning Module\\Building_Defect_AI\\outputs\\reports\\experiment3_evaluation.json\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import json\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import classification_report, accuracy_score\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create report directory\n",
    "REPORT_DIR = ROOT / \"outputs\" / \"reports\"\n",
    "REPORT_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Calculate final metrics\n",
    "accuracy = accuracy_score(y_true, y_pred)\n",
    "\n",
    "report = classification_report(\n",
    "    y_true,\n",
    "    y_pred,\n",
    "    target_names=class_names,\n",
    "    output_dict=True,\n",
    "    zero_division=0\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Save results\n",
    "results = {\n",
    "    \"model\": \"ResNet18 Experiment 3\",\n",
    "    \"architecture\": \"ResNet18\",\n",
    "    \"dataset\": \"BD3\",\n",
    "    \"num_classes\": len(class_names),\n",
    "    \"test_images\": len(y_true),\n",
    "    \"test_accuracy\": accuracy,\n",
    "    \"class_names\": class_names,\n",
    "    \"classification_report\": report\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "report_path = REPORT_DIR / \"experiment3_evaluation.json\"\n",
    "\n",
    "with open(report_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
    "    json.dump(results, f, indent=4)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Test accuracy: {accuracy:.4%}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Test images: {len(y_true)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Results saved: {report_path}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1f700574",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Conclusion\n",
    "\n",
    "Report the measured test accuracy and per-class recall from this run. Compare with Experiment 1 (83.14%) and Experiment 2 (79.75%), noting that fair comparison requires the same test split and evaluation procedure. Do not copy a previously mentioned Experiment 3 score without reproducing it here."
   ]
  }
